## Program compliance
### iTrust Special Alt Doc — Self-Employed Option 2: 1099
Guideline: products/itrust/Special Alt Doc 04.27.26.pdf

| Requirement | Required | Actual | Margin | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Min FICO (80% LTV tier) | 680 | 738 (EX 741 / EQ 738 / TU 735) | +58 | ✅ Pass |
| Max LTV (purchase, SFR ≤$1M) | 80% | 80.00% | 0 (at ceiling) | ✅ Pass |
| Max CLTV | 80% | 80.00% (no 2nd lien) | 0 | ✅ Pass |
| Max DTI | 50% | 40.5% (10% factor) / 43.4% (locked CPA P&L) | +9.5 / +6.6 | ✅ Pass |
| Loan amount | $100K – $3,000,000 | $460,000 | — | ✅ Pass |
| Reserves | 3 mo PITIA = $11,127 | $137K post-liquidation (surplus +$3,873) | +$3,873 | ⚠️ Verify (liquidation unproven) |
| Tradelines | 3×12mo or 2×24mo | 4 tradelines, all >12mo | — | ✅ Pass |
| First-time homebuyer | Allowed | Yes (no ownership ≤3 yrs) | — | ✅ Pass |
| Credit events | BK 3yr / FC 5yr / DIL 2yr; no multiples | None | — | ✅ Pass |
| Continuous self-employment | ≥2 yrs | ~4 yrs (start 08/2022) | +2 yrs | ✅ Pass |
| 1099 business-owner exclusion | Owner paying own earnings via 1099 = ineligible | Contractor via staffing agencies + direct clients | — | ✅ Pass |
| Property / occupancy / citizenship | SFR · Primary · US Citizen | All met | — | ✅ Pass |
| 1099 Tax Transcripts | Required | Not ordered | — | ⚠️ Pending |
| WVOE + YTD verification | Required (≤30 days of Note) | Not received | — | ⚠️ Pending |
| Licensed Tax Preparer 2-yr letter | Required | Expense letter on file; 2-yr history unconfirmed | — | ⚠️ Verify |

Note on income: under Option 2, P&L/tax returns are **not required** — qualifying income = 1099 gross × 0.90. The CPA P&L on file is supporting documentation used to lock a *more conservative* method; both pass the 50% cap.

