### Income
Qualifying income is the decisive variable. The program's actual method is **more favorable** than the LO's locked figure.

| Method | Basis | Income/yr | Income/mo | Back-end DTI | vs 50% cap |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **iTrust Option 2 (1099, 10% factor)** | $145,000 × 0.90 | $130,500 | $10,875 | 40.5% | ✅ Pass |
| Option 1 (P&L, most-recent 12-mo net) | $145,000 − $18,000 | $127,000 | $10,583 | 41.6% | ✅ Pass |
| **LO-locked CPA P&L (2-yr avg net)** | $138,500 − $17,000 | $121,500 | $10,125 | 43.4% | ✅ Pass |
| Hypothetical 25% factor (not in program) | $138,500 × 0.75 | $103,875 | $8,656 | 50.8% | ❌ Fail |

Calculation chain (— analyst:income-analyzer):
- 2025 1099 gross **$145,000**: Insight Global (Microsoft) $85K + Kelly Services (Amazon) $42K + Qualcomm $12K + Sony $4K + other small clients $2K — clients/chang/2-income/1099-nec-*.pdf
- 2024 1099 gross **$132,000** (Insight Global $78K + Kelly $38K + direct $16K) — clients/chang/2-income/1099-summary-2024.pdf
- 2-yr avg gross **$138,500**; YoY trend **+9.8%** (rising) — analyst:income-analyzer
- CPA P&L (Thompson & Associates, CA CPA #089421, dated 07/28/2026): 2025 net **$127,000** ($145K − $18K); 2024 net **$116,000** ($132K − $16K); 2-yr avg net **$121,500**. 2025 expenses $18K = home office $6K / equipment-software $4K / subscriptions $3K / dev-certs $3K / E&O insurance $2K. Note the intake's "~$17K expenses" is the 2-yr average; 2025 alone is $18K. — clients/chang/2-income/cpa-profit-loss.pdf, analyst:income-analyzer
- Program Option 2 formula: 1099 gross × 0.90 = $130,500 ($10,875/mo) — products/itrust/Special Alt Doc 04.27.26.pdf (p.8)
- The LO's stated DTI (43.1% / 50.4%) uses ~$650 installment-only obligations and PITIA $3,710; the table above uses $690 (incl. $40 card min) and PITIA $3,708.96 — same conclusions. — clients/chang/6-notes/intake-update-0813.txt, calc:dti-analyzer
- Caveat: direct-client 1099s are combined on one statement ($18K) — individual 1099s for Qualcomm/Sony not on file. — analyst:income-analyzer
- If WVOE validates YTD below $145K, qualifying income steps down. — products/itrust/Special Alt Doc 04.27.26.pdf (p.8)

